---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import Fill from '@/components/Fill.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
const L = site.legal;
const g = L.grievanceOfficer;
const toc = [
  ['who', 'Who we are'], ['scope', 'Scope'], ['collect', 'Information we collect'], ['purposes', 'Why we use it'],
  ['consent', 'Consent and withdrawal'], ['files', 'Design files'], ['sharing', 'Sharing'], ['transfers', 'Transfers outside India'],
  ['retention', 'Retention'], ['security', 'Security'], ['rights', 'Your rights'], ['cookies', 'Cookies and analytics'],
  ['children', 'Children'], ['grievance', 'Grievance Officer'], ['changes', 'Changes'],
].map(([id, label]) => ({ id, label }));
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Nanofab Innovations Pvt. Ltd. collects, uses, shares and protects personal data, and your rights under Indian law." toc={toc}>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how {site.legalName} ("<strong>Nanofab</strong>", "<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>us</strong>") handles personal data
    collected through this website. We process personal data in accordance with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the rules made under it
    (together, the "<strong>DPDP Act</strong>"), the Information Technology Act, 2000 and other applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    For the purposes of the DPDP Act, Nanofab is the <em>Data Fiduciary</em> for personal data collected through this website.<br />
    {site.legalName}, CIN: <Fill value={L.cin} label="CIN" /><br />
    Registered office: <Fill value={L.registeredAddress} label="Registered address" />
  </p>

  <h2 id="scope">2. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers personal data you share when you browse this website, submit an enquiry or product request, or upload a Bill of Materials (BOM) or
    other files. Services we deliver under a contract may be covered by additional terms in that contract.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">3. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact and enquiry details you provide:</strong> name, company or organisation, email address, phone number, country, the service or product
      you are interested in, and your project description.</li>
    <li><strong>Files you upload:</strong> BOMs, schematics, Gerber files, drawings and other project documents. These may contain the names or contact details of
      your staff.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> our hosting provider automatically processes basic technical information such as IP address, browser type and
      requested pages, to deliver and secure the website. If analytics is enabled, see <a href="#cookies">Cookies and analytics</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not ask for sensitive personal data such as financial account details, health information or biometrics through this website. Please do not include such data in your submissions.</p>

  <h2 id="purposes">4. Why we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your enquiry and communicate with you about it.</li>
    <li>To review your requirements and files and to prepare quotations, including checking component availability.</li>
    <li>To provide the products or services you ask for, if you choose to proceed.</li>
    <li>To keep the website secure and working properly, and to prevent misuse.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use enquiry details for unrelated marketing without your separate consent.</p>

  <h2 id="consent">5. Legal basis, consent and withdrawal</h2>
  <p>
    We process the personal data you submit on the basis of your consent, which you give by ticking the consent box on our forms, and where otherwise permitted
    by law (for example, to comply with legal obligations). You may withdraw consent at any time by writing to
    <Fill value={L.privacyEmail || g.email} label="privacy email" />. Withdrawal does not affect processing already carried out, but we may no longer be able
    to respond to your enquiry or complete a quotation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="files">6. Design files and confidential information</h2>
  <p>
    Files you upload remain your property. We use them only to evaluate your request, prepare quotations and, if you engage us, deliver the work.
    Access is limited to personnel and partners who need it for those purposes. If you require a Non-Disclosure Agreement before sharing details,
    mention this in your enquiry and we will arrange one before you send files.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">7. Who we share information with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers (Data Processors)</strong> who help us run the website and our communications, such as hosting, form handling and email
      providers. They act on our instructions under contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Manufacturing and component supply partners</strong>, only where needed to quote for or fulfil your request, and under confidentiality obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, where required by law or a lawful order.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="transfers">8. Transfers outside India</h2>
  <p>
    Some service providers or supply partners may process data outside India. Any such transfer is made in accordance with the DPDP Act, including any
    restrictions notified by the Government of India.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">9. How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry data and uploaded files only as long as needed for the purposes above. If an enquiry does not lead to an engagement, we delete or
    anonymise it within a reasonable period, unless a longer period is required by law. Records relating to an engagement are kept as required by
    applicable accounting, tax and legal requirements.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">10. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable security practices and procedures, including encrypted connections (HTTPS) and access controls, to protect personal data against
    unauthorised access, loss or misuse. In the event of a personal data breach, we will notify the Data Protection Board of India and affected individuals
    as required by the DPDP Act.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">11. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to the DPDP Act, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>obtain a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how we use it;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected or updated;</li>
    <li>have your personal data erased when it is no longer needed for the purpose it was collected for, unless retention is required by law;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent;</li>
    <li>nominate another person to exercise these rights in the event of death or incapacity; and</li>
    <li>have your grievances addressed by our Grievance Officer and, if unresolved, complain to the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise these rights, contact us using the details in section 14. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">12. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising cookies. We may use website analytics to understand how visitors use the site, for example which pages are viewed.
    Where an analytics tool would set non-essential cookies or similar identifiers, we ask for your consent first through a banner, and you can change your choice
    at any time using the "Cookie settings" link in the footer. Privacy-friendly analytics that do not use cookies or identify individuals may run without a banner.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">13. Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is intended for businesses and professionals and is not directed at individuals under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal data from
    children. If you believe a child has submitted data to us, please contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="grievance">14. Grievance Officer and contact</h2>
  <p>
    In accordance with the DPDP Act and the Information Technology Act, 2000 and rules made under it, questions, requests and complaints about personal data
    can be addressed to:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong><Fill value={g.name} label="Grievance Officer name" /></strong>, {g.designation}<br />
    {site.legalName}<br />
    Email: <Fill value={g.email} label="Grievance Officer email" /><br />
    {g.phone && <>Phone: {g.phone}<br /></>}
    Address: <Fill value={L.registeredAddress} label="Registered address" />
  </p>
  <p>We aim to acknowledge grievances promptly and to resolve them within the timelines required by applicable law.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">15. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows the latest version. Significant changes will be highlighted on this page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
